 of <b>electricity</b>. Amount which is mentioned in the provisional <b>assessment</b> has been treated as final <b>assessment</b> without affording any <b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b> and without", "docsize": 6638, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Allahabad High Court"}, {"tid": 161649524, "catids": null, "doctype": 1008, "publishdate": "2021-01-22", "authorid": null, "bench": [2045, 82], "title": "Harendra Kumar Sharma vs State Of U.P. And 3 Others on 22 January, 2021", "numcites": 2, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "<b>assessment</b>, <b>hearing</b> and final <b>assessment</b> in case of theft of <b>electricity</b>. Amount which is mentioned in the provisional <b>assessment</b> has been treated as final <b>assessment</b> ... without affording any <b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b>, the same is in violation of principles of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b>. \n  \n Considering the facts and circumstances of the case", "docsize": 6479, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Allahabad High Court"}, {"tid": 155495176, "catids": null, "doctype": 1008, "publishdate": "2021-01-25", "authorid": null, "bench": [2045, 82], "title": "Suman vs State Of U P And Another on 25 January, 2021", "numcites": 2, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "<b>assessment</b>, <b>hearing</b> and final <b>assessment</b> in case of theft of <b>electricity</b>. Amount which is mentioned in the provisional <b>assessment</b> has been treated as final <b>assessment</b> ... without affording any <b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b>, the same is in violation of principles of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b>. \n  \n Considering the facts and circumstances of the case", "docsize": 5716, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Allahabad High Court"}, {"tid": 115494498, "catids": null, "doctype": 1008, "publishdate": "2021-02-12", "authorid": null, "bench": [2045, 82], "title": "Mujaffar vs State Of U P And 3 Others on 12 February, 2021", "numcites": 2, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "<b>assessment</b>, <b>hearing</b> and final <b>assessment</b> in case of theft of <b>electricity</b>. Amount which is mentioned in the provisional <b>assessment</b> has been treated as final <b>assessment</b> ... without affording any <b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b>, the same is in violation of principles of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b>. \n  \n In this view of the matter, we dispose", "docsize": 4886, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Allahabad High Court"}, {"tid": 98162459, "catids": null, "doctype": 1008, "publishdate": "2021-01-18", "authorid": null, "bench": [2045, 82], "title": "Lokesh Mittal Alias Romi vs State Of U.P. And 3 Others on 18 January, 2021", "numcites": 2, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "<b>assessment</b>, <b>hearing</b> and final <b>assessment</b> in case of theft of <b>electricity</b>. Amount which is mentioned in the provisional <b>assessment</b> has been treated as final <b>assessment</b> ... without affording any <b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b>, the same is in violation of principles of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b>. \n  \n Considering the facts and circumstances of the case", "docsize": 6670, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Allahabad High Court"}, {"tid": 133617305, "catids": null, "doctype": 1008, "publishdate": "2021-01-25", "authorid": null, "bench": [2045, 82], "title": "Nijamuddin vs State Of U P And 3 Others on 25 January, 2021", "numcites": 2, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "<b>assessment</b>, <b>hearing</b> and final <b>assessment</b> in the case of theft of <b>electricity</b>. In the present case, amount which is mentioned in the provisional <b>assessment</b> ... treated as final <b>assessment</b> without affording any <b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b>, hence, the same in in violation of principles of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b>. \n  \n Considering the facts", "docsize": 5965, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Allahabad High Court"}, {"tid": 64028698, "catids": [1], "doctype": 1007, "publishdate": "2019-09-17", "authorid": 1385, "bench": [1385], "title": "M.Ashokan vs The District Collector on 17 September, 2019", "numcites": 1, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "second\n\n                     respondent has issued no objection certificate for getting <b>electricity</b>\n\n                     connection and for the <b>assessment</b> of property tax. Learned counsel\n\n                     appearing for the petitioner would ... <b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b> to\n\n                     the petitioner and hence, the same is liable to be set aside as it\n\n                     violates the principles of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b>", "docsize": 6083, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Madras High Court", "author": "T Raja", "authorEncoded": "t-raja"}, {"tid": 102204742, "catids": null, "doctype": 1024, "publishdate": "2014-09-19", "authorid": 1612, "bench": [1612], "title": "M/S Jatwani Udyog Ltd vs Dakshin Haryana Bijli Vitran Nigam Ltd ... on 19 September, 2014", "numcites": 2, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "principal grievance was\n                     against the non-observance of principles of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b> by\n                     the Assessing Authority a final order under  Section ... Chandigarh \n                       LPA No.1912 of 2014 (O&amp;M)                                    [2] \n\n                     given <b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b> to the appellant before passing\n                     the final order.\n                                   Such a plea", "docsize": 8292, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Punjab-Haryana High Court", "author": "S Kant", "authorEncoded": "s-kant"}, {"tid": 131762340, "catids": null, "doctype": 1006, "publishdate": "2015-04-24", "authorid": 592, "bench": [592], "title": "Omebati Devi Agarwal vs Unknown on 24 April, 2015", "numcites": 1, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "provisional <b>assessment</b> and that\n\nas such the allegation to the effect that there has been violation\n\nof the principles of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b>, is not sustainable ... petitioner to the effect that she was\n\nnot   granted   reasonable    <b>opportunity</b>    of   <b>hearing</b>   by   the\n\nrespondent no.2 does not stand reflected in the averments", "docsize": 4966, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Calcutta High Court (Appellete Side)", "author": "T Chakraborty", "authorEncoded": "t-chakraborty"}, {"tid": 192506490, "catids": null, "doctype": 1005, "publishdate": "2008-07-01", "authorid": 539, "bench": [539], "title": "Smt. Sunita Chakraborty vs Cesc Limited & Anr on 1 July, 2008", "numcites": 1, "numcitedby": 0, "headline": "that   she   was    deprived     of\n\nreasonable <b>opportunity</b> of <b>hearing</b> prior to passing of the final\n\norder      of   <b>assessment</b>    appears    to   this    Court   to    be   justified ... were not furnished to her thereby resulting in\n\nviolation of <b>natural</b> <b>justice</b>. This Court is of the considered view\n\nthat interest of <b>justice</b> would", "docsize": 3549, "fragment": true, "docsource": "Calcutta High Court", "author": "D Datta", "authorEncoded": "d-datta"}], "found": "91 - 100 of 2291", "encodedformInput": "electricity%20assessment%20%22opportunity%20of%20hearing%22%20natural%20justice%20doctypes%3Ahighcourts"}